From 7d19dc50772ddc608f37c5c4124b38fde04cb484 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 18:44:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Gate difficulty policy on real per-child/global data, wire
 retrain trigger into BreathQuest & VaakMirror
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two real gaps, confirmed against origin/hf-deploy before writing anything:

1. tabular_q/ppo/recurrent_ppo were selectable with no check that there was
   ever enough real data behind them. A brand-new child's tabular_q ran on
   a simulator-seeded prior + 15% exploration from event 3 onward; ppo/
   recurrent_ppo would run the initial simulator-only checkpoint forever
   since nothing ever forced a retrain check outside Chime.

   agent/service.py: decide() now resolves an effective policy separately
   from the requested one. tabular_q downgrades to rule_based until a
   child has 20+ of their own logged events AND their own persisted
   Q-table exists. ppo/recurrent_ppo downgrade until a real (non-simulator)
   global retrain checkpoint exists. Response carries requested_policy +
   downgrade_reason so a downgrade is never silent.

   Caught and fixed a chicken-and-egg bug in my own first draft: a child's
   Q-table can only ever get persisted via the pending-transition tracked
   in the tabular_q execution branch, but a tableless child is always
   downgraded away from that branch under a strict AND gate — permanently
   locking every new child out, not just temporarily. Fixed by keeping the
   online Q-learner warming up in the background even while the response
   is served via rule_based.

2. breath_agent.py's log_breath_event and VaakMirror's
   _log_session_to_agent both wrote real events via data_store.add_event
   but never triggered any retrain check — only Chime's log_event did.

   Promoted chime.py's local _run_retrain_if_due + threading lock into a
   shared retraining/scheduler.run_retrain_if_due(db_path), exported via
   retraining/__init__.py, so all three games check/trigger against one
   lock instead of racing to retrain the same shared checkpoint. Wired it
   into breath_agent.py (new BackgroundTasks param) and VaakMirror's
   end_session -> _log_session_to_agent (BackgroundTasks threaded through
   the async path). chime.py switched to the shared function and dropped
   its now-dead local lock/threading import.

Also surfaced policy_used/requested_policy/downgrade_reason on VaakMirror's
therapist-facing GameSettingsSuggestion endpoint, matching the other two
games' AgentDecisionOut schemas.

Verified: all 8 files py_compile clean; retraining package and vaakmirror
schema chain import for real; routers/chime.py, routers/breath_agent.py,
vaakmirror/routers/sessions.py, vaakmirror/routers/game_settings.py all
import end-to-end against the real dependency chain (installed librosa/
parselmouth/scipy/asyncpg to get there) with source-level confirmation of
each new call site. Ran a synthetic test against real SQLite/JSON storage
(no mocks) walking every gate transition: <3 events, downgraded at 5
events/no table, table persists via the background-warm-up fix, still
downgraded at 5 events with a table, gate opens at 20+ events; ppo/
recurrent_ppo downgraded with no checkpoint, gate opens once one exists
(confirmed by reaching real model-loading code, which then fails only on
stable_baselines3/sb3_contrib not being installed in this sandbox).
